\[ \Delta H_f = \Delta H_{\text{comb}} - \text{Enthalpy of formation of Hg(g)} \]

Given \(\Delta H_{\text{comb}} = -173.36 \, \text{kJ/mol}\) and the enthalpy of formation of \(\mathrm{Hg}(g)\) is \(61.32 \, \text{kJ/mol}\), the enthalpy of formation for \(\mathrm{HgO}(s)\) is:  

\[ \Delta H_f = -173.36 \, \text{kJ/mol} - 61.32 \, \text{kJ/mol} = -234.68 \, \text{kJ/mol} \]

